## summary
- 60 Hz input: 60.001 completions/s, every input frame once (runs of 1; longer runs: source).
- 50 Hz: 60.000/s, runs 1,1,1,1,2: every fifth input frame twice. 29.97 Hz: every frame twice.
  25 Hz: runs 2,2,3,2,3 (2.4 per frame). 23.98 Hz: runs 2,3 (3:2 pulldown).
- No repeat marker: CH_STATUS[31:3] reads 0x8204 at every completion, new image or repeat; in
  0x300-0x3fc only CH_STATUS, CH_CTRL (0x304) and 0x33c change, all with the 4-slot rotation;
  in 0x1000-0x10fc only IN_FRAME_PERIOD (0x1010), by 1-2 ticks of jitter.
- RATE_CTRL at a 50 Hz input: [31:16] = 25, 30 or 50, bit 0 set, bit 3 set, bits 0 and 3 set:
  60.000 completions/s and 48-49 new images/s in every case. Bit 3 does not stick (written
  0x00320008, read 0x00320000); bit 0 does (0x00320001). Restored: bits 0 and 3 cleared (run 12).
- So delivery cannot follow the input rate with the registers tried, and nothing tells a
  repeated completion from a new one: the driver reports the delivered 60 Hz (1/60) for these
  inputs and keeps the detected DV timings.
